{"id": "EUVD-2026-81741", "enisaUuid": "8392c804-97e5-3515-a19f-37215e4edecd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nNFSv4: Fix incorrect argument passed to nfs4_delete_lease() in nfs4_add_lease()\n\nWhen nfs4_add_lease() races with a delegation return, it calls\nnfs4_delete_lease() to clean up. Previously, it passed priv,\nwhich can legitimately be NULL. Passing a NULL priv eventually\nleads to a NULL pointer dereference in generic_setlease().", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:50:05", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e25e5b4a764638ec9e2dc6c9affe080c922ea1f2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff7244faa13b23e9acfad9df0438f0b44b338f62", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d148a652d52fd6aee96daf798922eb800ebb3018", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d179ff22cd8514f966966fd9ad425dcbb98e1ada", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/468e458ffde907ba19acd2102ca1fbb8f6fbede2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90148", "GHSA-h59h-gp4w-wvx7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02420d5a-750a-3ff9-9a76-25943e6385d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "0fb1d0c1-94e6-3c37-93cf-8e547d5bd0aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "2fecbdfa-9305-3c1d-b487-d4e3b6f08d99", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e93a5e9306a576011f03011b492d4fbaa274477b <d179ff22cd8514f966966fd9ad425dcbb98e1ada"}, {"id": "5a356488-4933-3b7b-b613-2943a806b077", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "663eef58-5dc5-3ea7-8efa-a1c5c5b23f8e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e93a5e9306a576011f03011b492d4fbaa274477b <468e458ffde907ba19acd2102ca1fbb8f6fbede2"}, {"id": "7526f48d-2a69-3aeb-9eb2-5bf7dbfe388